WEBVTT

00:35.883 --> 00:38.553
Oh, Brian, we're so thrilled
your gay cousin, Jasper,

00:38.677 --> 00:40.302
finally decided to come visit.

00:40.385 --> 00:41.887
Me, too. It's been way too long.

00:42.013 --> 00:43.015
Anyway, thanks for putting him up.

00:43.139 --> 00:44.224
No problem, Brian.

00:44.348 --> 00:45.348
It's great to have visitors.

00:45.473 --> 00:47.518
Except for that time
Moby-Dick stayed with us.

00:47.600 --> 00:49.603
Do you have any Raisin Bran?

00:49.728 --> 00:51.937
Uh, oh, no, sorry.

00:53.314 --> 00:55.316
Well, can you go get me some?

00:55.566 --> 00:57.899
Uh, boy, that's kind of a pain in the...

00:57.983 --> 00:59.402
We do have...

00:59.485 --> 01:01.151
We got Total, and we got some raisins.

01:01.235 --> 01:03.155
I mean, you could,
like, mix those together.

01:03.238 --> 01:04.613
I mean, it would be kind
of like Raisin Bran.

01:04.740 --> 01:05.865
Mmm, yeah, but it's not.

01:05.949 --> 01:08.284
It would be like Raisin Bran,
but it's not Raisin Bran.

01:08.410 --> 01:09.703
That would be like Total with raisins in it.

01:09.783 --> 01:11.034
That's just splitting hairs here.

01:11.117 --> 01:13.078
It's not really doing it for me.

01:13.620 --> 01:15.874
What time did you say your flight was?

01:19.000 --> 01:22.004
Oh, no locks.
Thank you, Homeland Security.

01:23.586 --> 01:26.172
Hey, bud, take a break.
I'll take over. Go smoke a fatty.

01:26.255 --> 01:27.507
Thanks.

01:28.255 --> 01:30.384
<i>This is
Sierra Tango 817,</i>

01:30.467 --> 01:31.719
<i>Matthew McConaughey's private jet,</i>

01:31.845 --> 01:33.095
<i>requesting permission to land.</i>

01:33.219 --> 01:34.389
Matthew McConaughey?

01:34.511 --> 01:36.347
Oh, sorry, Sierra Tango 817.

01:36.431 --> 01:37.472
All our runways are filled.

01:37.598 --> 01:40.435
<i>But it looks empty from up here.
We're almost out of fuel.</i>

01:40.561 --> 01:41.727
No, no. No room at all.

01:41.850 --> 01:43.687
But, lucky for you,
there's a big, new airport

01:43.770 --> 01:45.021
out in the middle of the ocean.

01:45.104 --> 01:46.148
Keep going. You can't miss it.

01:46.273 --> 01:47.396
<i>Roger that.</i>

01:48.856 --> 01:50.607
Oops. Well, look at it this way.

01:50.734 --> 01:53.234
I just got you on next year's
Oscar telecast.

01:53.359 --> 01:55.737
You'll be right after Ron Howard!

01:55.819 --> 01:57.030
Just messing with you, Ron.

01:57.113 --> 01:58.699
Or maybe not!

01:58.782 --> 02:00.031
No, seriously, I am.

02:00.115 --> 02:01.116
Or am I?

02:01.241 --> 02:02.451
No.

02:02.867 --> 02:04.203
Oh, there's Jasper's plane.

02:04.287 --> 02:05.660
- Where?
- Third one in line.

02:05.785 --> 02:08.121
Oh, it's one of them new niche airlines.

02:14.001 --> 02:15.502
Hey, Cousin!

02:15.628 --> 02:17.213
Hey, Jasper!

02:17.297 --> 02:20.716
Everybody, this is Ricardo,
from the Philippines and my kitchen floor.

02:20.799 --> 02:21.925
How was your flight?

02:22.008 --> 02:24.342
Oh, torture!
Five hours on my moneymaker,

02:24.467 --> 02:27.221
sitting across from a gaggle of sailors
flying home on leave.

02:27.304 --> 02:28.931
Here I am in a committed relationship,

02:29.014 --> 02:31.222
and all I can think about
is having a piece of Navy cake.

02:31.306 --> 02:33.892
"Hello. Who's that on the phone?"
"Temptation!"

02:33.975 --> 02:35.811
How does he
always get my number? I don't know.

02:35.937 --> 02:39.438
Anyway, I got big news,
and I'll tell you over dinner. Greek. On me.

02:39.522 --> 02:40.899
But enough about last weekend.

02:40.981 --> 02:42.313
I'm terrible!

02:42.439 --> 02:44.732
This idiot
will fit in with our family

02:44.816 --> 02:47.028
as badly as Peter
fit in with The Proclaimers.

03:06.957 --> 03:08.626
I'm singing! I'm singing!

03:13.172 --> 03:15.591
Hey, Chris, this field trip
is your chance, man.

03:15.674 --> 03:17.469
Alyssa is all alone.

03:19.258 --> 03:22.807
She's so pretty that if your Hacky Sack
were my private parts,

03:22.930 --> 03:24.851
I'd let her do that to them.

03:24.933 --> 03:26.765
What? Kick them around?

03:26.849 --> 03:29.812
Um, wait. Yes.

03:30.187 --> 03:32.521
<i>Welcome, citizens.
Today we commemorate</i>

03:32.604 --> 03:37.026
<i>those brave Quahog soldiers
who perished in the recent Gulf conflict.</i>

03:37.152 --> 03:40.028
<i>I can think
of no greater tribute to their memories</i>

03:40.109 --> 03:42.071
<i>than this solid gold statue</i>

03:42.196 --> 03:45.614
<i>of Dig 'Em, the Sugar Smacks frog.</i>

03:45.698 --> 03:46.992
What is that?

03:47.075 --> 03:51.535
<i>The spirit of America
is epitomized by his inspiring motto,</i>

03:51.618 --> 03:54.038
<i>'"Smack, smack, Sugar Smack.</i>

03:54.120 --> 03:56.831
<i>'"Give me a smack,
and I'll smack you back. '"</i>

03:58.083 --> 03:59.917
<i>I'd also like to take this opportunity</i>

04:00.043 --> 04:01.838
<i>to announce extreme budget cutbacks</i>

04:01.920 --> 04:05.422
<i>having almost nothing to do
with this solid gold statue.</i>

04:07.340 --> 04:10.217
Have you ever seen
such a waste of the taxpayers' money?

04:10.301 --> 04:11.719
You're talking to me!

04:11.802 --> 04:13.469
This is more exciting than that time

04:13.553 --> 04:15.220
me and my friends did mushrooms.

04:15.346 --> 04:17.180
This is gonna be awesome!

04:17.264 --> 04:18.515
You said it.

04:20.185 --> 04:22.059
Man, you guys feel anything yet?

04:22.184 --> 04:23.643
I feel kind of funny.

04:23.727 --> 04:25.104
I got a bellyache.

04:25.230 --> 04:26.857
We shouldn't have did this, man.

04:30.525 --> 04:33.401
Lois, darling, those earrings are delicious.
Total kitsch.

04:33.484 --> 04:35.112
Like an Andy Warhol wet dream.

04:35.236 --> 04:38.072
I'm opening a museum
and putting you in it, they're that fabulous.

04:38.197 --> 04:40.198
You think it's clever
talking like that, do you?

04:40.281 --> 04:41.366
You think it's funny?

04:41.492 --> 04:43.451
Talking about earrings, and using words

04:43.578 --> 04:45.786
like "fabulous" and "delicious" and "wet. "

04:45.910 --> 04:47.204
What's next? A workout

04:47.329 --> 04:49.998
followed by a romp around a crowded room
while the music goes...

04:55.086 --> 04:56.464
Oh, why did you stop?

04:56.587 --> 04:57.878
Hey, Jasper, let me ask you something.

04:58.003 --> 04:59.880
When you're in the shower at the "Y,"

04:59.964 --> 05:02.383
<i>is that just like
Supermarket Sweep for you guys,</i>

05:02.467 --> 05:03.719
or is there some kind of etiquette?

05:03.802 --> 05:05.300
Peter, stop it.

05:05.426 --> 05:07.346
God! You're more clueless than Popeye.

05:07.429 --> 05:10.221
Sir, I think you should know
these growths on your forearms,

05:10.304 --> 05:11.556
they're giant tumors.

05:12.765 --> 05:13.808
Oh, dear.

05:13.933 --> 05:15.518
Yeah, I'm surprised you haven't realized

05:15.603 --> 05:17.728
this is not how a human being
is supposed to look.

05:20.230 --> 05:22.982
And the speech thing,
and what you're doing with your eye...

05:23.107 --> 05:25.568
Uh, you had a stroke
about seven years ago.

05:27.153 --> 05:29.736
That you've managed
to be walking around all this time

05:29.820 --> 05:31.698
is nothing short of a miracle.

05:32.740 --> 05:34.201
I'd say about two months.

05:34.283 --> 05:36.492
Okay, all right,
time for the big announcement.

05:36.618 --> 05:40.036
Everyone, Ricardo and I
are getting married!

05:40.162 --> 05:41.705
Oh, that is terrific!

05:41.788 --> 05:43.289
It's about time you two settled down.

05:43.373 --> 05:44.416
Oh, you hear that, Meg?

05:44.500 --> 05:46.126
Guys can marry other guys now.

05:46.251 --> 05:48.835
So... This is awkward, but, uh,

05:48.961 --> 05:52.380
I mean, if they can do that,
that's pretty much it for you, isn't it?

05:52.464 --> 05:55.175
I mean, you might as well pack it in.
Game over.

05:58.302 --> 05:59.593
Alyssa, hi.

05:59.843 --> 06:03.932
I was wondering if maybe you wanted
to do something sometime?

06:04.015 --> 06:04.975
Sure, Chris.

06:05.100 --> 06:07.810
I have a Young Republicans
meeting after school. You wanna come?

06:07.933 --> 06:11.229
Oh, sure. What do you do at
a Young Republicans meeting?

06:11.312 --> 06:14.064
We help those who already have
the means to help themselves.

06:14.145 --> 06:16.108
Also, we perpetuate the ideal

06:16.191 --> 06:19.359
that Jesus chose America
to destroy nonbelievers and brown people.

06:19.483 --> 06:22.904
I don't understand what you're saying,
but somehow I feel safer.

06:27.658 --> 06:28.827
Karl, this is Chris.

06:28.950 --> 06:30.079
He wants to join our club.

06:30.158 --> 06:31.451
Karl is our chancellor.

06:31.576 --> 06:33.329
Well, Chris, we'd be happy to have you.

06:33.454 --> 06:35.873
There's just one little rite of initiation.

06:55.637 --> 06:57.848
Liberal chubby chaser!

06:59.141 --> 07:00.851
Well, if you can't laugh at yourself...

07:05.688 --> 07:08.189
I'm here at the parking lot
outside city hall,

07:08.312 --> 07:10.191
where hundreds of citizens
have come out in protest

07:10.316 --> 07:13.442
of the Mayor's decision to spend
the town's treasury on a gold frog.

07:13.526 --> 07:14.986
I don't like it.

07:15.070 --> 07:18.364
And I don't like
the contraction apostrophe-E-M.

07:18.489 --> 07:21.826
As far as I'm concerned,
his name is Dig Them.

07:21.907 --> 07:24.077
You're not welcome here, Dig Them.

07:24.204 --> 07:25.911
I stand behind my decision.

07:26.035 --> 07:27.913
This press conference is over.

07:28.037 --> 07:30.832
I can't see you now.
I can't hear you now. You're not here now.

07:34.169 --> 07:36.589
Well, there you have it. Back to you, Tom.

07:39.881 --> 07:41.883
Thanks, Tom. Some damn fine reporting.

07:42.007 --> 07:43.384
Damn fine. Diane?

07:43.718 --> 07:45.425
Well, it's encouraging to know

07:45.551 --> 07:48.848
that I'm not the only Mayor West
who's facing difficulties.

07:48.971 --> 07:51.349
But what I need now is a diversion.

07:51.430 --> 07:52.599
Let's see.

07:59.188 --> 08:01.314
Mmm. "Jingle keys. "

08:06.735 --> 08:09.361
My God! I'm a tomato!

08:11.739 --> 08:14.534
<i>And now back to
The Sound of Music.</i>

08:22.246 --> 08:23.540
Oh, thank heaven.

08:23.665 --> 08:25.208
The von Trapp family escaped!

08:25.291 --> 08:27.249
Reverend Mother, I have sinned.

08:27.375 --> 08:29.377
What is this sin, my child?

08:30.671 --> 08:32.129
Oh, well. No harm done.

08:32.254 --> 08:33.923
I too have sinned, Mother.

08:34.090 --> 08:35.592
Oh, my God!

08:35.675 --> 08:36.633
That's Rolfe!

08:36.759 --> 08:38.260
What the hell is wrong with you?

08:38.385 --> 08:40.760
Hey, I didn't start this war, but it's on!

08:42.053 --> 08:43.556
Oh, Lois, there you are.

08:43.638 --> 08:45.392
Listen, Ricardo and I wanna thank you

08:45.476 --> 08:47.141
for letting us have the wedding here.

08:47.266 --> 08:49.894
Oh! You're having the wedding here?

08:50.020 --> 08:52.269
Yeah. I hope that's okay, Lois.
I offered them the house.

08:52.394 --> 08:55.273
Oh, uh, sure. No problem.

08:55.606 --> 08:57.360
Hey, McButt the Crime Dog,

08:57.443 --> 08:59.860
I heard you and your little chew toy
getting it on last night.

08:59.944 --> 09:00.986
Keep it down.

09:01.111 --> 09:02.069
Sorry, little man.

09:02.153 --> 09:03.572
Ricardo and I were playing Clue,

09:03.656 --> 09:06.114
and he got me in the bedroom
with a lead pipe.

09:06.197 --> 09:07.908
Peter, I'm not sure I'm comfortable

09:07.992 --> 09:09.618
having this wedding at the house.

09:09.745 --> 09:12.245
Lois, I don't know what the big deal is.
So they're gay.

09:12.329 --> 09:15.873
It's not like we're gonna have
a gay sex orgy in the living room.

09:18.833 --> 09:20.460
That's not what I'm talking about.

09:20.585 --> 09:22.379
I've got nothing against homosexuals.

09:22.463 --> 09:24.880
I mean, I'll watch anything
with David Schwimmer.

09:24.964 --> 09:28.424
But the idea of two men
actually getting married,

09:28.508 --> 09:30.090
it just doesn't seem right.

09:30.174 --> 09:31.676
Hey, I say who cares, you know?

09:31.801 --> 09:34.137
If gays wanna get married
and be miserable like the rest of us,

09:34.262 --> 09:35.304
I say we should let them.

09:35.428 --> 09:36.889
Oh, no!

09:37.014 --> 09:38.306
- What's wrong?
- Look.

09:38.432 --> 09:41.060
<i>Some breaking news today
when Mayor West announced he will sign</i>

09:41.140 --> 09:43.685
<i>a citywide ban
on gay marriages next week.</i>

09:43.811 --> 09:45.271
<i>While controversial, it has nonetheless</i>

09:45.396 --> 09:48.272
<i>effectively distracted all of us
from the Dig 'Em fiasco.</i>

09:48.356 --> 09:50.441
<i>- The what?
- I don't know. Something about a lizard.</i>

09:50.566 --> 09:51.901
<i>And now this.</i>

09:51.985 --> 09:52.986
<i>Look at that.</i>

09:53.110 --> 09:55.612
<i>In the '30s, they called this
an Uncle Spinny Dervish.</i>

09:55.695 --> 09:57.364
<i>- Really?
- I don't know. I'm just bored.</i>

09:57.489 --> 10:00.198
A ban on gay marriage? Oh, my God!

10:02.617 --> 10:03.952
Matthew McConaughey?

10:04.036 --> 10:05.827
Yeah, I'm looking for a guy named Stewie.

10:06.995 --> 10:08.621
Chris, grab his legs. I gotta bury this thing.

10:08.747 --> 10:10.665
- But I...
- Grab his legs!

10:17.296 --> 10:19.631
I can't believe the wedding's off.

10:19.713 --> 10:21.340
All I ever wanted was to get married

10:21.466 --> 10:23.885
and make a home
with a skinny, hairless Filipino boy.

10:24.010 --> 10:25.427
Isn't that the American dream?

10:25.508 --> 10:26.927
Oh, don't give up yet, Jasper.

10:27.011 --> 10:28.723
Mayor West only banned gay marriage

10:28.847 --> 10:30.804
so he could distract
from the Dig 'Em scandal.

10:30.930 --> 10:32.265
He won't get away with it.

10:32.349 --> 10:34.475
Oh, Jasper, where'd you get
these brownies?

10:34.601 --> 10:37.143
They're from a bakery
in the West Quahog gay district.

10:37.269 --> 10:39.187
I thought they'd help my depression.

10:39.270 --> 10:43.607
Oh, I can see why. Oh, my God,
they pack so much fudge into these.

10:43.691 --> 10:46.277
And look at this. There's even
a couple of nuts lodged in there.

10:46.361 --> 10:47.652
I'm going upstairs.

10:47.735 --> 10:49.111
Oh, I've got to do something.

10:49.194 --> 10:51.614
Jasper's always
been there for me when I've needed him.

10:51.698 --> 10:54.033
I am gonna make Mayor West
change his mind.

10:54.159 --> 10:57.827
But, Brian, the Bible says
gay marriage is an abomination.

10:57.909 --> 10:59.913
Oh, don't give me
that Young Republican crap, Chris.

11:00.036 --> 11:02.495
The Bible also says
a senior citizen built an ark

11:02.621 --> 11:04.708
and rounded up two of every animal.

11:06.960 --> 11:08.544
- Hey.
- Yeah?

11:08.668 --> 11:10.210
What the hell is this?

11:10.671 --> 11:13.963
Oh, you didn't really give
any specific guidelines about mating.

11:14.046 --> 11:15.257
- Did you name it?
- What?

11:15.383 --> 11:16.383
Did you name it?

11:16.508 --> 11:17.886
Uh, yeah, he's Paul.

11:18.010 --> 11:20.092
Yeah? Well, it's gonna be
a hell of a lot harder for you now,

11:20.218 --> 11:22.429
because he's going the fuck overboard.

11:24.014 --> 11:24.973
Hi, Glenn.

11:25.098 --> 11:26.808
Uh, hey, will you sign
a petition to overturn

11:26.891 --> 11:28.518
Mayor West's ban on gay marriage?

11:28.643 --> 11:30.229
Gay marriage? Oh, come on,

11:30.353 --> 11:32.018
two halves can't make a whole
without a hole.

11:32.102 --> 11:33.396
Giggity Giggity Giggity Giggity.

11:39.276 --> 11:41.570
You get off my property, you pervert.

11:41.944 --> 11:44.737
Uh, Mr. Bottomtooth,
would you like to sign the petition?

11:47.783 --> 11:50.826
Uh, I don't... What's the problem?

11:54.956 --> 11:56.541
Ah! Okay. Thank you.

12:13.846 --> 12:15.015
Chris, did you hear?

12:15.094 --> 12:18.431
Some dog is going around town
trying to get support for gay marriage.

12:18.557 --> 12:20.684
Oh, that's Brian. He's got a petition.

12:20.768 --> 12:21.807
Really?

12:21.934 --> 12:23.768
Chris, you've got to destroy that petition.

12:23.894 --> 12:24.855
Why?

12:24.978 --> 12:27.563
Because if you do,
I'll let you touch my boobs.

12:27.688 --> 12:30.566
Is that good? Do I want that?

12:30.650 --> 12:32.235
Oh, yeah, you want that.

12:32.359 --> 12:33.983
Well, fantastic then.

12:36.237 --> 12:37.948
How can I help you, Mrs. Griffin?

12:38.073 --> 12:40.239
Well, I'm having a bit of a crisis.

12:40.323 --> 12:42.076
I'm a very open-minded person,

12:42.159 --> 12:44.744
and I've never
had any problem with gays before,

12:44.827 --> 12:48.496
but something about
two gay people getting married,

12:48.622 --> 12:50.123
I just don't think it's right.

12:50.249 --> 12:51.834
Well, these questions are too big

12:51.960 --> 12:53.457
to be decided by human beings.

12:53.583 --> 12:55.918
Which is why God made this film.

13:00.714 --> 13:03.927
You know, there's been
a lot of talk lately about homosexuals,

13:04.052 --> 13:05.968
but how do you know what to believe?

13:06.092 --> 13:10.265
Well, here are a few tips that
may help you tell when you've got a gay.

13:10.596 --> 13:12.933
So, uh, what's your favorite
Madonna album?

13:13.056 --> 13:14.267
I like her early work.

13:14.350 --> 13:17.435
<i>If his answer
is anything but '"I've never bought one, '"</i>

13:17.560 --> 13:19.437
<i>you've got a gay.</i>

13:19.687 --> 13:22.274
Let's take a blood sample, Mr. Braga.

13:22.524 --> 13:26.277
<i>If instead of human blood,
you find a deadly corrosive acid,</i>

13:26.361 --> 13:28.278
<i>you've got a gay.</i>

13:35.951 --> 13:38.286
<i>Not this time, nancy-boy.</i>

13:40.662 --> 13:42.578
Well, that was interesting.

13:42.662 --> 13:45.208
<i>I also have My Giant with Billy Crystal.</i>

13:45.333 --> 13:46.835
Oh, God, no, no.

13:50.336 --> 13:52.255
Well, we almost have enough signatures,

13:52.339 --> 13:54.005
thanks to Quahog's gay district.

13:54.130 --> 13:57.009
Lois, how'd you like to be
signature number 10,000?

13:57.092 --> 13:59.511
- Brian, I can't sign this.
- Why not?

13:59.595 --> 14:02.512
Well, because I don't believe
in gay marriage.

14:02.638 --> 14:04.889
You don't believe...
Lois, that's ridiculous.

14:05.015 --> 14:06.640
Gay people have every right
to get married.

14:06.766 --> 14:09.018
Well, they certainly
have every right to be together,

14:09.144 --> 14:11.437
but marriage should be
between a man and a woman.

14:11.521 --> 14:13.812
Well, that's not how they
do it in West Quahog.

14:13.896 --> 14:15.856
By the way, Lois,
I got a piercing over there.

14:15.940 --> 14:18.151
I'm not gonna tell you where,
but I'll give you a hint.

14:18.236 --> 14:21.069
It wasn't my nose or my ear
and it was one of my balls.

14:21.194 --> 14:22.570
Well, regardless of what you think,

14:22.697 --> 14:24.323
this is going to change
Mayor West's mind,

14:24.448 --> 14:26.281
and we are gonna have
Jasper's wedding here.

14:26.364 --> 14:29.408
Fine. Then until this is all over,
I'll stay somewhere else.

14:29.533 --> 14:31.661
Come on, Stewie, we're going
to Grandma and Grandpa's.

14:31.744 --> 14:34.328
Fine, I'll go,
but I'm not missing that gay wedding.

14:34.454 --> 14:35.748
I still kick myself for missing

14:35.873 --> 14:37.080
that topless cheerleader parade

14:37.205 --> 14:38.915
with the 100-foot chocolate teddy bear

14:39.041 --> 14:40.667
and the F-16s doing aerial acrobatics,

14:40.793 --> 14:42.629
choreographed to the music of Queen.

14:42.713 --> 14:44.378
Oh, I remember that day.

14:45.630 --> 14:47.923
Huh. Should have gone to that thing.

14:53.554 --> 14:55.804
My petition! What the hell are you doing?

14:55.887 --> 14:58.598
I'm going to get to touch
right-wing boob because of this.

14:58.724 --> 15:01.515
You idiot! Now I'm going to have
to get 10,000 more signatures

15:01.599 --> 15:03.727
before tomorrow morning.
What were you thinking?

15:03.852 --> 15:05.604
You don't understand, Brian.

15:05.730 --> 15:08.188
When was the last time
you were even with a woman?

15:08.314 --> 15:11.276
<i>- Uh, when did the Challenger blow up?
- '86.</i>

15:11.399 --> 15:13.816
Yeah, it was like three years before that.

15:16.278 --> 15:18.906
Mayor West, here's the gay marriage ban
for your approval.

15:19.032 --> 15:20.949
Excellent. This is so important,

15:21.074 --> 15:22.909
I'm going to sign it with all capital letters.

15:23.034 --> 15:26.535
It's going to say, "ADAM WEST."

15:26.703 --> 15:28.705
That's what it's going to say, you'll see.

15:28.788 --> 15:30.541
Hey, buddy, you can't go in there.

15:31.876 --> 15:33.334
Mayor West, you have to look at this.

15:33.458 --> 15:34.918
Ten thousand signatures.

15:35.002 --> 15:36.335
I've been up for 24 hours,

15:36.419 --> 15:37.546
I paid off a few people

15:37.629 --> 15:40.631
and I did a few things
in West Quahog I'm not proud of.

15:46.093 --> 15:49.222
So, it's a show
about three hookers and their mom?

15:49.306 --> 15:52.557
This is very impressive,
but my decision stands.

15:53.265 --> 15:54.268
No!

15:54.394 --> 15:55.935
Come on, buddy, you're leaving.

15:56.060 --> 15:58.310
No, I can't let Jasper down.

15:59.770 --> 16:01.147
I'm not going to let you sign that.

16:01.273 --> 16:02.859
Go on, get out of here.

16:04.942 --> 16:08.027
I should warn you,
I have a tiny bullet-proof shield,

16:08.111 --> 16:11.989
the exact size of a bullet,
somewhere on my body.

16:12.113 --> 16:16.493
And if you hit it, I'll be unharmed,
and your plan will be foiled.

16:16.617 --> 16:19.203
You'll be the laughingstock of me.

16:19.287 --> 16:20.998
I don't want to shoot you, Mayor West.

16:21.122 --> 16:23.080
Good, because I'm incredibly crafty.

16:23.204 --> 16:25.249
Hey, what's that on the ceiling?

16:26.459 --> 16:27.833
Now I'm over here.

16:33.758 --> 16:35.966
Look, this has gotten out of hand, I know.

16:36.091 --> 16:37.676
I don't want anyone to get hurt.

16:37.801 --> 16:39.345
But you can put an end to this right now

16:39.470 --> 16:41.302
by tearing up that gay marriage ban.

16:41.428 --> 16:42.595
You won't break me.

16:42.679 --> 16:45.223
15 years ago
I swallowed everything I needed

16:45.307 --> 16:47.515
to escape from a hostage situation.

16:54.854 --> 16:55.941
A wall!

16:56.023 --> 16:56.983
Well, no matter.

16:57.108 --> 17:00.110
I'm prepared
for a lengthy captivity as well.

17:02.905 --> 17:06.239
<i>I swallowed this People magazine in 1989.</i>

17:06.657 --> 17:11.035
<i>All right, Paul Hogan,
tell me about the real Crocodile Dundee.</i>

17:13.996 --> 17:16.499
It's so nice to have you home, dear.

17:16.582 --> 17:17.749
I can take it or leave it.

17:17.831 --> 17:20.210
God, this is such
an old-people house, you know.

17:20.334 --> 17:21.293
I mean, look at this candy jar.

17:21.419 --> 17:22.838
Let's, uh, take a look in here.

17:22.963 --> 17:24.920
Let's see what you got here. You got...

17:25.005 --> 17:27.633
You got licorice. Oh, that's, uh, that's...

17:27.716 --> 17:29.339
Oh, Freedent. Oh, that's good.

17:29.464 --> 17:31.383
Yeah, I got a sweet tooth,

17:31.509 --> 17:33.469
I think I'll have some Freedent.

17:33.552 --> 17:35.223
What's this? A cough drop.

17:35.348 --> 17:36.679
A Luden's cough drop.

17:36.804 --> 17:40.475
Is that candy? No, I don't think
that's candy. I think it's a cough drop!

17:40.600 --> 17:42.768
What else we got? Look. Look at this.

17:42.850 --> 17:44.644
There's a fishing lure in here.

17:44.770 --> 17:47.524
There's a fishing lure in the candy jar.

17:47.649 --> 17:50.483
What?
Am I supposed to eat this?

17:50.732 --> 17:53.569
Eat a fishing lure?
Hey, look, Brian's on TV.

17:53.694 --> 17:55.986
<i>And now,
some Channel five exclusive footage</i>

17:56.111 --> 17:57.655
<i>of the crazed homosexual gunman</i>

17:57.739 --> 17:59.323
<i>who's taken Mayor West hostage.</i>

17:59.448 --> 18:00.573
Oh, my God!

18:00.698 --> 18:02.367
Brian's taken the Mayor hostage?

18:02.493 --> 18:04.411
Is this an eyeglass lens?

18:04.536 --> 18:07.371
I didn't realize
how strongly he feels about this.

18:07.494 --> 18:08.664
Gay marriage.

18:08.788 --> 18:10.249
Next thing you know, they'll want to vote.

18:10.373 --> 18:11.416
Oh, oh, look at this.

18:11.541 --> 18:14.669
A spare key for a Volkswagen Scirocco.

18:14.794 --> 18:16.503
They don't even make this anymore.

18:16.627 --> 18:18.753
They don't even make this car anymore.

18:18.878 --> 18:20.924
Whose key could this possibly be?

18:21.047 --> 18:22.383
What if Brian's right?

18:22.508 --> 18:26.009
I mean, certainly the love between a man
and a woman should be sacred, but...

18:26.134 --> 18:28.346
Who's talking about love?
We're talking about marriage.

18:28.428 --> 18:29.930
Well, don't you love Mom?

18:30.056 --> 18:31.346
Come on, Lois, look at her.

18:31.472 --> 18:33.474
So two straight people
who hate each other

18:33.557 --> 18:35.101
have more of a right to be together

18:35.227 --> 18:36.854
than two gay people who love each other?

18:36.938 --> 18:39.063
That's what we raised you to believe.

18:39.187 --> 18:41.941
Oh, my God! I've made a terrible mistake!

18:42.106 --> 18:44.608
I've been brainwashed,
like Elizabeth Smart.

18:44.817 --> 18:46.985
It's so wonderful having her home again.

18:47.069 --> 18:48.905
She's brought music back into the house.

18:49.029 --> 18:50.778
Playing songs on the harp.

18:50.904 --> 18:54.075
Of course most of them
are about rape, but it's still nice.

18:55.077 --> 18:57.118
I think I made Brian crazy.

18:57.242 --> 18:59.079
Maybe I shouldn't have burned
that petition.

18:59.204 --> 19:01.289
No, Chris, you did the right thing.

19:01.414 --> 19:04.206
It's only a matter of time
before Mayor West signs that bill,

19:04.331 --> 19:06.043
and you'll get to touch these.

19:06.127 --> 19:09.126
Oh, boy, I got a feeling that
before the end of the day,

19:09.252 --> 19:11.046
I'm going to be burying my dog.

19:11.129 --> 19:14.130
Whoa, whoa. I said you could touch
my boobs. Let's start with that.

19:14.255 --> 19:17.091
Look, Peter, if you can't get Brian
to come out peacefully,

19:17.218 --> 19:18.552
we're going to have to take him down.

19:18.636 --> 19:20.887
Don't worry, Joe,
I'm good with tight situations.

19:21.011 --> 19:23.348
Like when I saved Luke Skywalker's life.

19:23.765 --> 19:25.892
Okay, Luke, this will keep you warm

19:26.017 --> 19:27.973
until I get the shelter built.

19:31.312 --> 19:32.560
You're sure this is okay?

19:32.686 --> 19:34.188
Yeah, you're just cutting into the fat.

19:34.271 --> 19:36.399
<i>All right, Brian, Peter's coming in.</i>

19:37.359 --> 19:39.941
I'll relax him by using my catchphrase.

19:41.070 --> 19:43.531
Hey, what's up with you?

19:46.531 --> 19:48.283
- What the hell was that?
- My catchphrase.

19:48.409 --> 19:49.534
You don't have a catchphrase.

19:49.618 --> 19:52.120
Why you gotta say like that?

19:53.870 --> 19:55.290
Excuse me.

19:56.832 --> 19:58.790
Would anyone like to play Stratego?

19:58.874 --> 20:00.293
I have Stratego.

20:00.377 --> 20:02.045
Oh, Peter, I never meant
for this to happen.

20:02.126 --> 20:05.714
This whole situation
has totally spiraled out of control.

20:05.796 --> 20:08.674
<i>Brian, listen to me. I was wrong.</i>

20:08.800 --> 20:12.636
<i>If two people love each other,
they should have the right to get married.</i>

20:12.760 --> 20:15.222
<i>But you have to come down
and give yourself up.</i>

20:15.306 --> 20:16.929
<i>If you drag this out any longer,</i>

20:17.013 --> 20:19.099
<i>you're only hurting your own cause.</i>

20:20.809 --> 20:23.393
She's right. I'm sorry, Mayor West.

20:23.476 --> 20:26.231
Well, you were only doing
what you thought was right, Brian.

20:26.313 --> 20:29.397
And, hey, you've distracted everyone
from the Dig 'Em statue,

20:29.481 --> 20:32.444
so I guess we don't need this bill anymore.

20:36.152 --> 20:38.614
Everybody happy!

20:47.661 --> 20:51.167
Well, it sure was nice of Mayor West
to drop the kidnapping charges.

20:51.292 --> 20:53.166
It's amazing. All he asked for in return

20:53.292 --> 20:55.168
was the key to a Volkswagen Scirocco.

20:55.293 --> 20:56.461
You're welcome.

20:56.544 --> 20:57.712
Listen, Lois,

20:57.838 --> 21:00.046
I really appreciate
you putting your discomfort aside,

21:00.171 --> 21:01.507
so we could have the wedding here.

21:01.631 --> 21:03.635
Oh, please, I'm over all that now.

21:03.717 --> 21:06.301
Two men getting married
doesn't bother me in the least.

21:06.426 --> 21:07.845
They deserve happiness.

21:07.970 --> 21:10.305
Everybody gay!

21:10.306 --> 22:11.306
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru